WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.033 --> 00:00:02.200
-Welcome back to "Late Night."

00:00:02.200 --> 00:00:03.534
We're here with John Oliver.
Very exciting.

00:00:03.534 --> 00:00:05.501
We are going to be spending
New Year's Eve together.

00:00:05.501 --> 00:00:06.667
-Yeah we are.
We're going to be doing

00:00:06.667 --> 00:00:08.734
stand-up in Las Vegas.
-Yeah, we are.

00:00:08.734 --> 00:00:10.200
[ Audience cheers ]

00:00:10.200 --> 00:00:11.901
-And you've noticed
that it's very funny,

00:00:11.901 --> 00:00:13.501
the room they have us
doing stand-up in.

00:00:13.501 --> 00:00:16.033
-Yes, because
it's Adele's theater.

00:00:16.033 --> 00:00:17.567
[ Laughter ]

00:00:17.567 --> 00:00:21.734
And so for one night only Adele
ain't going to be there.

00:00:21.734 --> 00:00:23.601
And I hope that's made
very clear

00:00:23.601 --> 00:00:26.434
to the people that turn up
to that theater.

00:00:26.434 --> 00:00:28.667
-And it's just you and Adele
are this Venn diagram

00:00:28.667 --> 00:00:30.734
where just a tiny slice
of British...

00:00:30.734 --> 00:00:34.167
[ Laughter ]

00:00:34.167 --> 00:00:36.434
That's it. Just like...
-That's it. That's it.

00:00:36.434 --> 00:00:39.167
That's it.

00:00:39.167 --> 00:00:40.501
-I'm fascinated.

00:00:40.501 --> 00:00:41.901
I mean, you do New Year's Eve
shows every year.

00:00:41.901 --> 00:00:43.367
-Yeah, I love it.
-And you've always said

00:00:43.367 --> 00:00:45.534
it's the best way to spend New
Year's, and you've been kind.

00:00:45.534 --> 00:00:47.100
-Yeah, because you're not
really spending it.

00:00:47.100 --> 00:00:49.801
You're kind of basically
doing something else instead.

00:00:49.801 --> 00:00:51.267
It's classic
displacement activity, right?

00:00:51.267 --> 00:00:52.534
-Yeah.
-So I love it.

00:00:52.534 --> 00:00:56.033
I hate New Year's
as an evening, I hate it.

00:00:56.033 --> 00:00:58.033
And so now I do stand-up,
which I love,

00:00:58.033 --> 00:01:00.234
and they cancel each other out.
It's great.

00:01:00.234 --> 00:01:01.601
-I'm very excited to be
doing it with you.

00:01:01.601 --> 00:01:03.367
Our friend Brooks Wheelan
will be there as well.

00:01:03.367 --> 00:01:04.567
-Yes, he's going to be there.
-Literally

00:01:04.567 --> 00:01:06.000
the greatest person
to be on the road with.

00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:07.133
You're on the road with him
all the time.

00:01:07.133 --> 00:01:08.801
-Yeah. He's the absolute
greatest, funniest,

00:01:08.801 --> 00:01:11.367
nicest, fantastic human being.
-Where do you think

00:01:11.367 --> 00:01:12.467
we'll be at midnight?

00:01:12.467 --> 00:01:14.567
-[ Laughing ]

00:01:14.567 --> 00:01:18.334
I mean, listen,
the high-percentage guess

00:01:18.334 --> 00:01:20.667
is back in our rooms alone.
-Yeah.

00:01:20.667 --> 00:01:21.868
[ Laughter ]

00:01:21.868 --> 00:01:23.200
-But having --
-That's what the money --

00:01:23.200 --> 00:01:25.567
That's what house money is on.
-House money is saying

00:01:25.567 --> 00:01:27.367
having a nice, quiet night,

00:01:27.367 --> 00:01:28.934
getting extra sleep
and getting an early flight

00:01:28.934 --> 00:01:31.133
out back to our families.
I will say, having said that,

00:01:31.133 --> 00:01:33.300
the tradition of coming
on this show

00:01:33.300 --> 00:01:37.534
and things turning out other
than I might otherwise imagine,

00:01:37.534 --> 00:01:39.200
there is a chance you're going
to be able to cut from this

00:01:39.200 --> 00:01:40.634
that it's just you and me
in our underwear,

00:01:40.634 --> 00:01:43.267
just running down the Strip,
unloading firearms in the air.

00:01:43.267 --> 00:01:45.534
-Yeah.
-We're golden gods!

00:01:45.534 --> 00:01:47.968
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:47.968 --> 00:01:50.667
2024 is going to be great!
Pow pow!

00:01:50.667 --> 00:01:52.734
-Pow pow! To the sphere!

00:01:52.734 --> 00:01:56.467
[ Laughter ]

00:01:56.467 --> 00:01:59.000
-Where's Bono?
-Yeah!

00:01:59.000 --> 00:02:00.467
-We find him.
-We find --

00:02:00.467 --> 00:02:02.467
-We got to find Bono.

00:02:02.467 --> 00:02:04.934
-There's nothing worse
than an English person saying,

00:02:04.934 --> 00:02:07.434
"Where's Bono?" with a gun
in his hand as well.

00:02:07.434 --> 00:02:09.667
[ Laughter ]

00:02:09.667 --> 00:02:13.033
"Bring me an Irishman!"
Yeah.

00:02:13.033 --> 00:02:16.868
-You and I, we were --
we podcasted together.

00:02:16.868 --> 00:02:18.234
-Yeah.
-Strike Force Five,

00:02:18.234 --> 00:02:20.234
which I heard
very nice things about.

00:02:20.234 --> 00:02:21.334
-Yeah.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:21.334 --> 00:02:25.801
Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:02:25.801 --> 00:02:27.567
-I didn't know if it would work
when we first started doing it.

00:02:27.567 --> 00:02:29.734
-I was almost sure it wouldn't.
-Yeah.

00:02:29.734 --> 00:02:31.934
-So, yeah, it's a very,
very pleasant surprise

00:02:31.934 --> 00:02:34.501
that it turned out okay.
People seem to like it.

00:02:34.501 --> 00:02:36.033
Even if I did wonder
that some people

00:02:36.033 --> 00:02:38.767
were listening with
a pathological interest.

00:02:38.767 --> 00:02:41.567
"Oh, wow. Let's just see
what these five lab rats do

00:02:41.567 --> 00:02:43.634
when they talk to each other."
[ Laughter ]

00:02:43.634 --> 00:02:44.968
-Or talk over each other.

00:02:44.968 --> 00:02:46.801
-That's right. Absolutely.
In many, many ways.

00:02:46.801 --> 00:02:49.667
-My favorite thing
about the podcast was,

00:02:49.667 --> 00:02:51.133
and I should say
we should both shout out.

00:02:51.133 --> 00:02:52.701
We've talked about it a lot.

00:02:52.701 --> 00:02:54.200
Jimmy Fallon
hosted episode five.

00:02:54.200 --> 00:02:55.667
-It's a masterpiece.
-It's a masterpiece.

00:02:55.667 --> 00:02:58.267
It's genuinely --
-I'm so grateful to him.

00:02:58.267 --> 00:03:01.234
I am so grateful to him
for what he gave us.

00:03:01.234 --> 00:03:03.901
I needed those laughs
so much at that point

00:03:03.901 --> 00:03:07.434
and only he could provide it.
It's just perfect.

00:03:07.434 --> 00:03:10.367
-It was a very poorly run

00:03:10.367 --> 00:03:13.133
and yet, because of that
exceptionally funny,

00:03:13.133 --> 00:03:15.801
basically "Newlywed Game"
where Fallon texted our wives.

00:03:15.801 --> 00:03:18.434
But we did find out super-fun
things about our wives,

00:03:18.434 --> 00:03:21.667
including the angriest you
ever were with your wife

00:03:21.667 --> 00:03:23.634
was when you went
to a pirate party.

00:03:23.634 --> 00:03:25.501
-Yeah.
-Pirate-themed party.

00:03:25.501 --> 00:03:28.234
-Yeah, because I dressed
like a pirate.

00:03:28.234 --> 00:03:30.968
-Yeah.
-And we were there first.

00:03:30.968 --> 00:03:33.667
And I remember
the host of the party

00:03:33.667 --> 00:03:35.868
not really being dressed
like a pirate and thinking,

00:03:35.868 --> 00:03:37.434
"oh, that's a shame,

00:03:37.434 --> 00:03:39.200
but at least there's lots of
pirates coming."

00:03:39.200 --> 00:03:41.868
[ Laughter ]

00:03:41.868 --> 00:03:43.267
Then...

00:03:43.267 --> 00:03:46.701
Then another couple turn up.
Very much not pirate-based,

00:03:46.701 --> 00:03:48.968
and I'm getting a sinking
feeling in my stomach

00:03:48.968 --> 00:03:51.901
saying, "The third one
will be the key here."

00:03:51.901 --> 00:03:54.234
Not dressed like a pirate.
And I really was dressed,

00:03:54.234 --> 00:03:56.267
like, very much like a pirate.

00:03:56.267 --> 00:03:59.534
-Yeah.
-So I spent a pretty angry

00:03:59.534 --> 00:04:03.133
afternoon and evening dressed
like a pirate among non-pirates.

00:04:03.133 --> 00:04:04.467
-Now, I also want to stress.

00:04:04.467 --> 00:04:06.667
I want to say even if everybody
dressed like a pirate...

00:04:06.667 --> 00:04:08.200
-Yes.
-...I'm going to go out

00:04:08.200 --> 00:04:09.834
on a limb and say you would
have hated that.

00:04:09.834 --> 00:04:11.000
-Yes.
-Yeah.

00:04:11.000 --> 00:04:14.534
-Oh, the evening was not
going to go great for me,

00:04:14.534 --> 00:04:19.701
but at least I wanted to be able
to be among other pirates,

00:04:19.701 --> 00:04:21.267
and I really wasn't.

00:04:21.267 --> 00:04:23.868
I was among people dressed
in kind of casual way.

00:04:23.868 --> 00:04:25.834
-And this is a photo
of you and your wife.

00:04:25.834 --> 00:04:27.934
And I do want to note
she's having a grand old time,

00:04:27.934 --> 00:04:32.033
and you are the unhappiest
I've ever seen a pirate.

00:04:32.033 --> 00:04:33.234
-Now, you say that.

00:04:33.234 --> 00:04:34.534
[ Laughter ]

00:04:34.534 --> 00:04:35.734
You say that.

00:04:35.734 --> 00:04:37.868
I would say...
[ Laughs ]

00:04:37.868 --> 00:04:41.267
I would say
a pirate on a pirate ship

00:04:41.267 --> 00:04:42.634
would look that unhappy

00:04:42.634 --> 00:04:44.734
if none of the other pirates
were dressed like pirates.

00:04:44.734 --> 00:04:47.033
[ Laughter ]

00:04:47.033 --> 00:04:50.300
-If it was like Casual Friday
on Pirates of the Caribbean.

00:04:50.300 --> 00:04:52.734
-That's right. Exactly.
You go, "Hey, guys.

00:04:52.734 --> 00:04:56.501
Guys, you have to let me know.
I've pirated up over here.

00:04:56.501 --> 00:04:59.300
You can't hang me out
to dry like this. Arrr."

00:04:59.300 --> 00:05:00.701
[ Laughter ]

00:05:00.701 --> 00:05:03.000
-Also an eyepatch
is even funnier

00:05:03.000 --> 00:05:04.400
when the pirate's
wearing glasses.

00:05:04.400 --> 00:05:09.000
[ Laughter ]

00:05:09.000 --> 00:05:10.968
-That is such a --

00:05:10.968 --> 00:05:13.400
And if you're wondering, is
an eyepatch more comfortable

00:05:13.400 --> 00:05:15.133
over the glasses
or under the glasses?

00:05:15.133 --> 00:05:17.601
It's a coin flip.
You just have to rotate.

00:05:17.601 --> 00:05:18.601
Neither is good.

00:05:18.601 --> 00:05:20.234
[ Laughter ]

00:05:20.234 --> 00:05:21.667
-Well, God love Kate.

00:05:21.667 --> 00:05:24.601
Also, it does feel like Kate's
goatee is also an eye patch.

00:05:24.601 --> 00:05:26.901
-Yes. That's right.

00:05:26.901 --> 00:05:28.934
-It does feel like you guys
bought a thing of iPads

00:05:28.934 --> 00:05:30.234
and you're like,
"We got to use them all."

00:05:30.234 --> 00:05:31.434
[ Laughter ]

00:05:31.434 --> 00:05:34.033
Whether it makes sense or not.
-That's right.

00:05:34.033 --> 00:05:35.934
Yeah. That's right.
Also, I just think

00:05:35.934 --> 00:05:38.000
she could get away
with it more than me.

00:05:38.000 --> 00:05:39.634
I don't know if it's the belt.

00:05:39.634 --> 00:05:41.133
If it's the Pirates
of the Caribbean.

00:05:41.133 --> 00:05:43.734
-Oh, everybody who's
seen this photo thinks that.

00:05:43.734 --> 00:05:46.200
[ Laughter ]

00:05:46.200 --> 00:05:47.467
You're like,
"Also, I'm going to say

00:05:47.467 --> 00:05:50.000
something you guys
might not have clocked.

00:05:50.000 --> 00:05:52.667
Kate makes a great pirate."
Yeah. No. We're there.

00:05:52.667 --> 00:05:54.033
[ Laughter ]

00:05:54.033 --> 00:05:55.701
I can't wait for
New Year's Eve, buddy,

00:05:55.701 --> 00:05:56.734
and hopefully
I'll see you before that.

00:05:56.734 --> 00:05:58.067
-I know. I never
thought I'd say that.

00:05:58.067 --> 00:06:00.167
-Yeah. No kidding.
John Oliver, everybody.

00:06:00.167 --> 00:06:03.000
"Last Week Tonight"
Sundays on HBO, streams on Max.

00:06:03.000 --> 00:06:05.634
We'll be right back with
Aaron Jackson and Josh Sharp.

